Q(12,4,2,"California: The speed limit at a blind intersection in California is","15 mph",["25 mph", "10 mph", "5 mph"],"If your view is blocked, move slowly forward until you can see.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: Near a railroad crossing where you cannot see the tracks for 400 feet in both directions, the California speed limit within 100 feet of the crossing is","15 mph",["25 mph", "10 mph", "35 mph"],"You may go faster only if the crossing has gates, a warning signal or a flagman.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, it is illegal for a driver over 21 to drive with a blood alcohol concentration of","0.08% or higher",["0.10% or higher", "0.05% or higher", "0.04% or higher"],"The limit is 0.04% for commercial drivers and drivers carrying a passenger for hire.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, it is illegal for a driver under 21 to drive with a blood alcohol concentration of","0.01% or higher",["0.02% or higher", "0.05% or higher", "0.08% or higher"],"The same 0.01% limit applies at any age to a driver on DUI probation.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, dim your high beams within how far of a vehicle coming toward you?","500 feet",["300 feet", "200 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Dim within 500 feet of an oncoming vehicle and within 300 feet of a vehicle you are following.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, dim your high beams within how far of a vehicle you are following?","300 feet",["500 feet", "200 feet", "100 feet"],"It is 300 feet when following and 500 feet for oncoming vehicles.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: California requires headlights beginning","30 minutes after sunset until 30 minutes before sunrise",["At sunset until sunrise", "One hour after sunset", "Only when street lights are on"],"You must also use them when it is too dark to see 1,000 feet ahead and whenever you need your wipers.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, if weather makes you use your windshield wipers, you must","Turn on your low-beam headlights",["Turn on your hazard flashers", "Use parking lights only", "Use high beams"],"Wipers on means headlights on.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, you should signal at least how far before a turn?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"On a freeway, signal at least five seconds before changing lanes.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: How far may you drive in a California center left turn lane?","200 feet",["100 feet", "500 feet", "One block"],"It is not a regular traffic lane or a passing lane.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, you may drive in a bike lane to make a turn only within how far of the intersection?","200 feet",["100 feet", "50 feet", "500 feet"],"Check for bicyclists in your blind spot before moving into the bike lane.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: A white painted curb in California means","Stop only long enough to pick up or drop off passengers",["No stopping at any time", "Parking for disabled persons only", "Park for a limited time"],"Green is limited-time parking and yellow is for loading passengers and freight.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: A green painted curb in California means","Park for a limited time",["No parking at any time", "Loading freight only", "Passenger pick-up only"],"The time limit is posted on a sign or painted on the curb.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "5 feet"],"The same 15 feet applies to a fire station driveway.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, you may not park within how many feet of a marked or unmarked crosswalk?","20 feet",["10 feet", "5 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 15 feet where the crosswalk has a curb extension.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: When you cannot change lanes to pass a bicyclist in California, you must leave at least","3 feet",["1 foot", "2 feet", "5 feet"],"If you cannot give three feet, wait until you can.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: During the first 12 months of a California provisional license, a driver under 18 may not drive between","11 p.m. and 5 a.m.",["Midnight and 5 a.m.", "10 p.m. and 6 a.m.", "9 p.m. and 5 a.m."],"The driver also may not carry passengers under 20 without a licensed adult, with limited exceptions.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: A California driver under 18 in the first 12 months may not carry passengers under what age without a qualified adult in the car?","20",["18", "21", "25"],"A parent, guardian or other California-licensed driver age 25 or older must be along.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: Before the driving test, a California teen must practice driving for at least","50 hours, 10 of them at night",["30 hours, 5 at night", "40 hours, none at night", "100 hours, 20 at night"],"The practice must be with a California-licensed driver who is at least 25.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: The minimum age to apply for a California instruction permit is","15½",["15", "16", "14"],"Applicants under 18 must also complete driver education.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: An adult California driver's license may be suspended for getting","4 points in 12 months",["2 points in 12 months", "3 points in 24 months", "10 points in 36 months"],"The totals are 4 points in 12 months, 6 in 24 months, or 8 in 36 months.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, it is illegal to leave a child of what age or younger alone in a vehicle?","6 years old",["4 years old", "8 years old", "10 years old"],"The child may be left with a person who is at least 12 years old.");
Q(12,4,2,"California: In California, when a minor is in the vehicle you may not","Smoke",["Play the radio", "Use the air conditioner", "Carry groceries"],"You can be fined for smoking with a minor in the vehicle.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: What score do you need to pass a Texas knowledge exam?","70 percent or better",["60 percent or better", "80 percent or better", "90 percent or better"],"The handbook says you must score 70 percent or better to pass any knowledge exam.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: Unless otherwise posted, the speed limit in a Texas urban district is","30 mph",["25 mph", "35 mph", "20 mph"],"The handbook's speed table lists 30 mph for an urban district.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: Unless otherwise posted, the speed limit in a Texas alley is","15 mph",["10 mph", "20 mph", "25 mph"],"Alleys are 15 mph, the same as beaches and county roads next to a public beach when the county declares it.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, a driver age 21 or over is legally intoxicated with a blood alcohol concentration of","0.08 or more",["0.10 or more", "0.05 or more", "0.04 or more"],"Fines can run as high as $10,000, not counting other costs.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: For a Texas driver under 21, a license suspension can follow from","Any detectable amount of alcohol",["A BAC of 0.02 or more only", "A BAC of 0.05 or more only", "A BAC of 0.08 or more only"],"Texas has zero tolerance for drivers under 21.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, it is illegal to have an open container of alcohol in the passenger area","Whether the vehicle is moving, stopped or parked on a public highway",["Only while the vehicle is moving", "Only if the driver is drinking", "Only at night"],"The fine can be up to $500.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, use low beams when you are within how far of an approaching vehicle?","500 feet",["300 feet", "200 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Also use low beams within 300 feet when following another vehicle.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, use low beams when following within how far of another vehicle?","300 feet",["500 feet", "100 feet", "200 feet"],"It is 300 feet when following and 500 feet for approaching vehicles.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: Texas requires headlights","From 30 minutes after sunset to 30 minutes before sunrise",["From sunset to sunrise", "Only after 9 p.m.", "Only outside cities"],"Also use them any time people or vehicles cannot be seen clearly for at least 1,000 feet.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, give a turn signal at least how far before you turn?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"Signal at least 100 feet before the turn.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 15 feet from a hydrant and 20 feet from a crosswalk at an intersection.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, you may not park within how many feet of a crosswalk at an intersection?","20 feet",["15 feet", "10 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 30 feet on the approach to a stop sign, yield sign or traffic signal.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, you may not park within how many feet of the approach to a stop sign or traffic signal?","30 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"The rule covers flashing signals, stop signs, yield signs and other traffic signals at the side of the road.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, you may not park within how many feet of the nearest rail of a railroad crossing?","50 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "100 feet"],"This applies whether or not the vehicle is occupied.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: When a Texas railroad signal warns of a train, you must stop how far from the nearest rail?","Between 15 and 50 feet",["Between 5 and 10 feet", "Between 50 and 100 feet", "At least 200 feet"],"Stay stopped until it is safe or you are allowed to proceed.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: A Texas school bus is stopped with alternately flashing red lights. You must","Stop, whichever direction you are coming from",["Stop only if you are behind the bus", "Slow to 10 mph and pass", "Honk and pass on the left"],"Wait until the bus moves, the driver signals you on, or the red lights stop flashing.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Texas, you do not have to stop for a school bus with flashing red lights when","You are on a different road or a controlled-access highway",["You are driving the opposite way on a two-lane road", "The bus is in a school zone", "It is after dark"],"In all other cases, stop from either direction.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: You approach a stopped emergency vehicle with lights on in Texas and cannot change lanes. Where the limit is 25 mph or more, you must slow to","20 mph less than the posted speed limit",["10 mph less than the posted limit", "5 mph less than the posted limit", "The posted limit"],"Where the limit is under 25 mph, slow to less than 5 mph.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: A Texas learner license applicant under 18 must be at least","15 years old",["14 years old", "15½ years old", "16 years old"],"The applicant must also complete the classroom part of driver education.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: A Texas driver under 18 must hold a learner license for at least how long before getting a provisional license?","Six months",["Three months", "Twelve months", "Nine months"],"A suspension during this phase extends the six months.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Phase Two of the Texas graduated license, a driver under 18 may not drive between","Midnight and 5:00 a.m.",["11:00 p.m. and 5:00 a.m.", "10:00 p.m. and 6:00 a.m.", "1:00 a.m. and 4:00 a.m."],"Exceptions are work, school activities and medical emergencies.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: In Phase Two of the Texas graduated license, a driver under 18 may carry no more than","One passenger under 21 who is not a family member",["Two passengers under 21", "Three passengers of any age", "No passengers at all"],"Family members do not count toward the limit.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: Texas drivers under 18 may use a wireless communication device","Only in an emergency, and hands-free devices are also banned",["Any time with a hands-free device", "Only at red lights", "Only on highways"],"The restriction covers hands-free devices too.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: The minimum liability insurance in Texas is","$30,000 per person, $60,000 per crash, $25,000 property damage",["$15,000 / $30,000 / $5,000", "$25,000 / $50,000 / $25,000", "$50,000 / $100,000 / $50,000"],"This is often written 30/60/25.");
Q(12,5,2,"Texas: The fine for a first conviction of driving without a license in Texas is","Up to $200",["Up to $50", "Up to $500", "Up to $1,000"],"A second conviction within a year is $25 to $200.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: The Florida Class E Knowledge Exam has how many multiple-choice questions?","50",["20", "25", "40"],"The questions cover Florida traffic laws, safe driving practices and traffic controls.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida's standard speed limit in a school zone is","20 mph",["15 mph", "25 mph", "30 mph"],"The handbook lists school zones at 20 mph.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida's standard speed limit on limited access highways is","70 mph",["65 mph", "75 mph", "55 mph"],"Always obey a lower posted limit.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, a driver 21 or older has the license suspended for a breath or blood alcohol level of",".08 or above",[".10 or above", ".05 or above", ".04 or above"],"Refusing the test also brings a suspension.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Under Florida's Zero Tolerance law, a driver under 21 is suspended for a blood alcohol level of",".02 or higher",[".05 or higher", ".08 or higher", ".01 or higher"],"The suspension is six months. At .05 or higher a substance abuse course is required.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, the first time you refuse a breath, blood or urine test your license is suspended for","One year",["30 days", "Six months", "Two years"],"A second refusal brings an 18-month suspension and a first degree misdemeanor.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, do not use high beams within how far of an oncoming vehicle?","500 feet",["300 feet", "200 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Also switch to low beams within 300 feet of a vehicle ahead of you.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, do not use high beams within how far of the vehicle ahead of you?","300 feet",["500 feet", "100 feet", "200 feet"],"It is 300 feet when following and 500 feet for oncoming vehicles.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida requires headlights","Between sunset and sunrise",["From 30 minutes after sunset", "Only after 8 p.m.", "Only on highways"],"Also turn on headlights whenever you turn on your windshield wipers.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, you must signal at least how far before making a turn?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"Signals are also required when changing lanes or passing.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 20 feet from an intersection and 30 feet from a stop sign or traffic signal.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, you may not park within how many feet of an intersection?","20 feet",["15 feet", "10 feet", "30 feet"],"The same 20 feet applies to the entrance of a fire, ambulance or rescue station.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, you may not park within how many feet of a stop sign or traffic signal?","30 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"It is 50 feet from a railroad crossing.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, you may not park within how many feet of a railroad crossing?","50 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"Never park where you block or create a hazard for other vehicles.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: When parked parallel in Florida, your right wheels must be within how far of the curb?","12 inches",["6 inches", "18 inches", "24 inches"],"Park in the direction of traffic, parallel to the curb.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida law requires you to give a bicyclist at least how much clearance when passing?","Three feet",["One foot", "Two feet", "Five feet"],"Also slow down and use caution when driving next to bicyclists.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A school bus stops ahead on a Florida highway divided by a raised barrier or an unpaved median at least five feet wide. If you are going the opposite direction, you","Do not have to stop, but proceed with caution",["Must stop until the stop signal is withdrawn", "Must stop for 30 seconds", "Must pull onto the shoulder"],"Painted lines are not a barrier. Drivers behind the bus must always stop.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A school bus stops on a Florida road divided only by painted lines. Drivers in both directions must","Stop until the stop signal is withdrawn and children are clear",["Slow to 10 mph", "Stop only if children are visible", "Proceed with caution"],"Painted lines or pavement markings are not considered barriers.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: On a Florida multi-lane road, you approach a stopped emergency or tow vehicle and cannot move over. You must slow to","20 mph below the posted speed limit",["10 mph below the posted limit", "5 mph below the posted limit", "Half the posted limit"],"If the limit is 20 mph or less, travel at 5 mph.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida's Move Over Law also covers","A disabled vehicle stopped with hazard lights on",["Only police cars", "Only vehicles on interstates", "Only school buses"],"It was expanded to disabled vehicles showing warning lights, flares or signs, or with people visibly present.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A Florida driver with a learner's license may drive, for the first three months,","Only during daylight hours",["Until 10 p.m.", "Until midnight", "At any hour"],"After three months, driving is allowed until 10 p.m. A licensed driver 21 or older must always be in the front seat.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A licensed 16-year-old in Florida may drive alone only between","6 a.m. and 11 p.m.",["5 a.m. and 1 a.m.", "6 a.m. and 10 p.m.", "7 a.m. and 9 p.m."],"Exceptions: driving to or from work, or with a licensed driver 21 or older.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A licensed 17-year-old in Florida may drive alone only between","5 a.m. and 1 a.m.",["6 a.m. and 11 p.m.", "6 a.m. and midnight", "5 a.m. and 10 p.m."],"Exceptions: driving to or from work, or with a licensed driver 21 or older.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: A Florida driver under 18 must hold a learner's license for","12 months or until age 18, whichever comes first",["6 months", "3 months", "18 months"],"The teen also needs 50 hours of driving experience, 10 of them at night.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, how many points within 12 months bring a 30-day license suspension?","12 points",["6 points", "8 points", "18 points"],"18 points in 18 months is a 3-month suspension; 24 points in 36 months is one year.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: In Florida, texting while driving adds how many points to your record?","3 points",["1 point", "4 points", "6 points"],"More points are added if the texting was in a school zone or caused a crash.");
Q(12,6,2,"Florida: Florida drivers must carry at least","$10,000 PIP and $10,000 property damage liability",["$25,000 bodily injury only", "$5,000 PIP only", "$50,000 combined coverage"],"Proof of insurance is required to register a vehicle.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: To pass the New York written test, you must correctly answer at least","14 of 20 questions, including 2 of the 4 road sign questions",["16 of 20 questions", "20 of 25 questions", "10 of 20 questions"],"You need 14 of 20 overall and at least two of the four questions about road signs.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: If no speed limit is posted in New York, you may drive no more than","55 mph",["50 mph", "65 mph", "45 mph"],"Often the safe speed is lower than the limit.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York City, turning right on a red light is","Not allowed unless a sign permits it",["Allowed after a full stop", "Allowed at any time", "Allowed only at night"],"Elsewhere in the state it is allowed after a stop unless a sign or signal prevents it.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, a blood alcohol content of .08 percent or higher is evidence of","Intoxication (DWI)",["Impairment only (DWAI)", "Aggravated DWI", "Nothing unless you crash"],"More than .05 is evidence of impairment, and .18 or more is aggravated DWI.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, a BAC of more than .05 percent is legal evidence that you are","Impaired",["Intoxicated", "Sober", "Guilty of aggravated DWI"],".08 or higher is evidence of intoxication.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, aggravated driving while intoxicated applies at a BAC of",".18 percent or more",[".08 percent or more", ".10 percent or more", ".15 percent or more"],"Aggravated DWI carries a minimum one-year revocation.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, headlights must be on low beam within how far of an oncoming vehicle?","500 feet",["200 feet", "300 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Also use low beams within 200 feet of a vehicle ahead of you.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, headlights must be on low beam within how far of a vehicle ahead of you?","200 feet",["500 feet", "300 feet", "100 feet"],"This applies even if the vehicle ahead is in a different lane.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: New York law requires headlights","From one-half hour after sunset to one-half hour before sunrise",["From sunset to sunrise", "Only after dark in cities", "Only on expressways"],"They are also required when visibility is under 1,000 feet and whenever you use your wipers.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, when you use your windshield wipers for rain, snow or sleet, you must also","Turn on your headlights",["Turn on your hazard lights", "Use high beams", "Slow to 25 mph"],"Wipers on means headlights on.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, you must signal a turn or lane change at least how far ahead?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"Use your turn lights or hand signals.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant, unless a licensed driver stays in the vehicle?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"A licensed driver must remain to move the vehicle in an emergency.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, parking is not allowed within how many feet of a crosswalk at an intersection?","20 feet",["15 feet", "10 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 30 feet from a traffic light, STOP sign or YIELD sign.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, parking is not allowed within how many feet of a traffic light, STOP sign or YIELD sign?","30 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"It is 20 feet from a crosswalk at an intersection.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, you may not make a U-turn where other drivers cannot see your vehicle from how far away?","500 feet",["200 feet", "100 feet", "1,000 feet"],"U-turns are also illegal in business districts of New York City.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: Under New York's Move Over Law, on a multi-lane controlled access road you must","Reduce speed and move from the lane next to the stopped vehicle if safe",["Only slow down", "Stop behind the vehicle", "Sound your horn and pass"],"The law covers emergency and hazard vehicles with their lights activated.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: Before the New York road test, you should have at least","50 hours of practice, 15 of them after sunset",["30 hours of practice, 5 after sunset", "20 hours of practice", "100 hours of practice, 25 after sunset"],"DMV also recommends 10 hours in moderate to heavy traffic.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: A New York junior permit must be held for at least how long before a road test can be scheduled?","Six months",["Three months", "Twelve months", "Nine months"],"Time when the permit is suspended or revoked does not count.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: With a New York junior learner permit, you generally may not drive with more than","One passenger under 21 who is not immediate family",["Two passengers under 21", "Three passengers of any age", "No passengers at all"],"The limit does not apply when the supervising driver is your parent, guardian or driving instructor.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, how many points does a texting or improper cell phone violation carry?","5 points",["2 points", "3 points", "8 points"],"Both improper cell phone use and texting are 5-point violations.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: A school bus is stopped with red lights flashing on the opposite side of a divided highway in New York. You must","Stop",["Slow down and proceed", "Proceed normally", "Stop only if children are crossing"],"New York requires you to stop even if the bus is on the opposite side of a divided highway.");
Q(12,7,2,"New York: In New York, you cannot park within how many feet of a railroad crossing?","50 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"It is 50 feet from a railroad crossing and 15 feet from a fire hydrant.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: How many questions are on the Pennsylvania knowledge test, and how many must you answer correctly?","18 questions, 15 correct",["20 questions, 16 correct", "25 questions, 20 correct", "50 questions, 40 correct"],"The manual says the Knowledge Test has 18 multiple-choice questions and you must answer 15 correctly.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A Pennsylvania permit holder under 18 must complete how many hours of behind-the-wheel practice before the road test?","65 hours",["40 hours", "50 hours", "100 hours"],"Under 18 you need at least 65 hours of supervised skill-building.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: Of the 65 practice hours for a driver under 18, how many must be at night and in bad weather?","10 hours at night and 5 hours in bad weather",["5 hours at night and 5 hours in bad weather", "15 hours at night and 10 hours in bad weather", "20 hours at night and none in bad weather"],"The 65 hours must include at least 10 nighttime hours and 5 bad-weather hours.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: How long must a driver under 18 hold a Pennsylvania learner's permit before taking the road test?","Six months",["Three months", "Thirty days", "One year"],"You must wait the mandatory six months from the permit issue date.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A Pennsylvania junior license holder may not drive between which hours without a parent, guardian or spouse 18 or older?","11 p.m. and 5 a.m.",["9 p.m. and 6 a.m.", "Midnight and 4 a.m.", "10 p.m. and 7 a.m."],"The junior license curfew is 11 p.m. to 5 a.m., with exceptions for work, volunteer fire service and charitable service.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A new Pennsylvania junior driver may carry how many passengers under 18 who are not immediate family, without a parent or guardian in the vehicle?","No more than one",["No more than three", "None at any time", "As many as there are seats"],"The junior license limits you to one passenger under 18 who is not immediate family unless a parent or guardian is with you.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania, when driving under 35 mph, you must signal at least how far before turning?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"Signal at least 100 feet before turning when driving less than 35 mph.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania, when driving 35 mph or faster, you must signal at least how far before turning?","300 feet",["100 feet", "150 feet", "500 feet"],"At 35 mph or more you must signal at least 300 feet before the turn.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: Pennsylvania law requires low beams when you are within how many feet of an oncoming vehicle?","500 feet",["300 feet", "200 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Use low beams within 500 feet of an oncoming vehicle.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: Pennsylvania law requires low beams when you are following another vehicle within how many feet?","300 feet",["500 feet", "100 feet", "150 feet"],"Use low beams when following a vehicle within 300 feet.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"Parking is not allowed within 15 feet of a fire hydrant.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania you may not park within how many feet of a crosswalk at an intersection?","20 feet",["10 feet", "15 feet", "30 feet"],"Parking is not allowed within 20 feet of a crosswalk at an intersection.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania you may not park within how many feet of a stop sign, yield sign or flashing signal?","30 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"Parking is not allowed within 30 feet of a flashing signal, stop sign, yield sign or traffic control device at the side of the road.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania you may not park within how many feet of the driveway entrance to a fire station?","20 feet",["10 feet", "30 feet", "50 feet"],"The manual lists 20 feet from a fire station driveway entrance.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: For a driver 21 or older in Pennsylvania, driving under the influence starts at what blood alcohol level?",".08",[".10", ".05", ".04"],"At .08 or higher an adult driver is considered to be driving under the influence. You can also be convicted at lower levels if you drive erratically.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A Pennsylvania driver under 21 is considered to be driving under the influence at what blood alcohol concentration?",".02 percent or more",[".08 percent or more", ".05 percent or more", ".04 percent or more"],"Pennsylvania has zero tolerance: .02 or more is DUI for a driver under 21.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: What happens the first time a Pennsylvania driving record reaches six or more points?","The driver gets a written notice to take a special point examination",["The license is cancelled for life", "Nothing until 12 points", "The driver must retake the road test only"],"At six or more points for the first time, PennDOT sends a notice to take a written special point examination.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A Pennsylvania junior driver gets a mandatory 90-day suspension for which of these?","Six or more points, or driving 26 mph or more over the limit",["Any single traffic ticket", "Two points on the record", "Driving after 9 p.m."],"Junior drivers are suspended for 90 days at six or more points or a conviction for 26 mph or more over the posted limit.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: What does Pennsylvania's Steer Clear law require when you approach an emergency response area?","Move into a lane that is not next to it",["Stop in your lane until waved on", "Speed up to clear the area", "Sound your horn and pass"],"The Steer Clear law requires moving to a lane that is not adjacent to the emergency response area. If you cannot move over, slow down.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: When a Pennsylvania school bus stops with red lights flashing and its stop arm out, you must stop at least how far away?","10 feet",["5 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"Stop at least 10 feet from the bus, whether you are behind it, coming toward it, or at an intersection where it is stopped.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: What is the speed limit in a Pennsylvania school zone when the yellow signals are flashing?","15 mph",["20 mph", "25 mph", "35 mph"],"You may travel no faster than 15 mph when the school zone signals are flashing or during the posted times.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: Speeding in a Pennsylvania school zone puts how many points on your record?","Three points",["One point", "Two points", "Six points"],"Exceeding the school zone speed limit results in three points.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: A new Pennsylvania resident with a valid out-of-state license must get a Pennsylvania license within how many days?","60 days",["30 days", "90 days", "10 days"],"You must get a Pennsylvania license within 60 days of moving and surrender the out-of-state license.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: What following distance does the Pennsylvania manual recommend?","4 seconds",["2 seconds", "1 second", "10 seconds"],"The manual teaches the 4-second rule to give time to steer or brake around a hazard.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: To avoid overdriving low-beam headlights on a dark road at night, the Pennsylvania manual says not to drive faster than","45 mph",["35 mph", "55 mph", "65 mph"],"Low beams light about 250 feet, so the manual advises no more than 45 mph on a dark road.");
Q(12,8,2,"Pennsylvania: In Pennsylvania you may not pass within how many feet of an intersection, railroad crossing, bridge or tunnel?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "500 feet"],"Passing is prohibited within 100 feet of an intersection or railroad crossing, bridge, elevated structure or tunnel unless a traffic control device allows it.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: How many questions are on the Ohio knowledge test, and what score passes?","40 questions, 75% to pass",["25 questions, 80% to pass", "50 questions, 70% to pass", "20 questions, 75% to pass"],"The manual says the test is 40 multiple-choice questions with a 75% pass rate, which is 30 correct.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: What is the minimum age to take the Ohio vision screening and knowledge test?","15 years and 6 months",["15 years", "16 years", "14 years and 6 months"],"At 15 years and six months you meet the minimum age for the vision screening and knowledge test.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: How many hours of driving must an Ohio permit holder under 18 log, and how many at night?","50 hours, with at least 10 at night",["40 hours, with at least 5 at night", "65 hours, with at least 10 at night", "30 hours, with at least 6 at night"],"Ohio requires 50 logged hours with a licensed driver, at least 10 of them at night.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: How long must an Ohio driver under 18 hold the temporary permit (TIPIC) before the driving test?","At least six months",["At least three months", "At least 30 days", "At least one year"],"Drivers under 18 must hold the TIPIC for at least six months.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: Ohio driver education for a driver under 18 includes how much instruction?","24 hours of classroom or online instruction and 8 hours of driving",["30 hours of classroom and 6 hours of driving", "12 hours of classroom and 12 hours of driving", "40 hours of classroom only"],"The course is 24 hours of classroom or online instruction plus 8 hours of driving time.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: An Ohio permit holder under 16 must have which person in the front passenger seat?","A parent, guardian, custodian, licensed instructor, or a person 21 or older acting in loco parentis",["Any licensed driver 18 or older", "Any passenger with a permit", "No one is required"],"Under 16, the supervising person must be a parent, guardian, custodian, licensed driving instructor, or a person 21 or older acting in loco parentis.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: During the first 12 months of holding an Ohio license, a driver under 18 may not drive during which hours without a parent or guardian?","Midnight to 6 a.m.",["10 p.m. to 5 a.m.", "11 p.m. to 5 a.m.", "1 a.m. to 4 a.m."],"In the first 12 months the driver may not drive from midnight to 6 a.m. unless with a parent or guardian, with exceptions such as work with documentation.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: During the first 12 months of holding an Ohio license, a driver under 18 may carry how many non-family passengers without a parent or guardian?","No more than one",["No more than two", "None", "As many as there are seats"],"The limit is one non-family passenger unless a parent or guardian is in the vehicle.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: For an Ohio driver under 18, how many people may ride in the vehicle?","No more than the number of safety belts originally installed",["Any number in the back seat", "No more than two", "No more than the driver's age allows"],"For drivers under 18, occupants are limited to the number of original safety belts, and everyone must wear one.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: In Ohio, a turn signal must be given at least how far before the turn?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "300 feet"],"Signal at least 100 feet before the intended turn or lane change.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: Ohio law requires headlights to be on at which of these times?","From sunset to sunrise and any time the wipers are in use because of precipitation",["Only when it is completely dark", "Only on highways at night", "Only when other drivers flash their lights"],"Headlights are required from sunset to sunrise, in poor visibility, and whenever wipers are in use because of precipitation.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: In Ohio, headlights must be on any time you cannot clearly see objects how far ahead?","1,000 feet",["500 feet", "300 feet", "100 feet"],"Lights must be on whenever natural light does not let you clearly see objects 1,000 feet ahead.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: On an Ohio road with fewer than four lanes, who must stop for a school bus picking up or dropping off students?","All traffic approaching from either direction, at least 10 feet from the bus",["Only traffic behind the bus", "Only traffic facing the bus", "No one if the bus is on the other side"],"On a road with fewer than four lanes, traffic from both directions must stop at least 10 feet from the bus and stay stopped until it moves or the driver signals.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: On an Ohio road with four or more lanes, who must stop for a stopped school bus?","Only traffic going the same direction as the bus",["All traffic in both directions", "Only traffic in the lane next to the bus", "No traffic has to stop"],"With four or more lanes, only traffic traveling in the same direction as the bus must stop.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: In Ohio you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","10 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "5 feet"],"Ohio prohibits parking within 10 feet of a fire hydrant.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: In Ohio you may not park within how many feet of an intersection or crosswalk?","20 feet",["10 feet", "30 feet", "50 feet"],"Parking is prohibited in or within 20 feet of an intersection or crosswalk.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: When a train is approaching an Ohio railroad crossing, where must you stop?","No closer than 15 feet and no farther than 50 feet from the crossing",["Right at the tracks", "At least 100 feet from the crossing", "Anywhere before the gate"],"Stop no closer than 15 feet and no farther than 50 feet from the crossing and wait until the train has passed and signals stop.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: What does Ohio's Move Over law require when you approach a stopped emergency or road service vehicle with warning lights on?","Move to an adjacent lane and/or slow down",["Stop behind it until it leaves", "Sound your horn and keep your speed", "Pass on the shoulder"],"Drivers must move over a lane when they can and slow down, proceeding with caution.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: For Ohio drivers 18 and older, which is illegal in most cases while driving?","Using, holding or physically supporting a cell phone",["Listening to the radio", "Talking to a passenger", "Using cruise control"],"Ohio's distracted driving law makes it illegal in most cases to use, hold or support a phone or other electronic wireless device while driving.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: How much space must an Ohio driver leave when passing a bicyclist?","At least three feet",["At least one foot", "At least six feet", "No set distance"],"Maintain a safety zone of at least three feet between your vehicle and the bicycle.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: A new Ohio resident must get an Ohio driver license within how many days of establishing residency?","30 days",["10 days", "60 days", "90 days"],"Within 30 days of establishing residency you must have an Ohio license; owned vehicles need Ohio title and registration.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: What following distance does the Ohio manual recommend between you and the vehicle ahead?","Four seconds, or one vehicle length for every 10 mph",["One second", "Two seconds at any speed", "Ten vehicle lengths at all times"],"The manual advises one vehicle length per 10 mph or four seconds.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: When may you turn right on a red light in Ohio?","After a complete stop and yielding, unless a sign prohibits it",["Never", "Only between midnight and 6 a.m.", "Without stopping if no cars are coming"],"You may turn right on red unless a sign prohibits it, after a full stop and after crossing traffic and pedestrians clear.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: Studded tires are legal in Ohio during which period?","November 1 through April 15",["October 1 through May 31", "December 1 through March 1", "All year"],"The manual says studded tires are legal from November 1 through April 15.");
Q(12,9,2,"Ohio: In Ohio, the slow-moving vehicle emblem on the rear of farm or animal-drawn vehicles means the vehicle is traveling","Less than 25 mph",["Less than 45 mph", "Exactly 35 mph", "At the speed limit"],"The emblem marks vehicles traveling less than 25 mph.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: How many questions must you answer correctly to pass each Georgia knowledge exam?","15 out of 20",["12 out of 20", "20 out of 25", "18 out of 20"],"The manual says you must correctly answer 15 out of 20 questions to pass. The road signs and road rules tests are scored separately.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: Before a Georgia Class D license, a teen must have how many hours of supervised driving, and how many at night?","40 hours, including 6 at night",["50 hours, including 10 at night", "30 hours, including 5 at night", "65 hours, including 10 at night"],"Georgia requires at least 40 hours of supervised driving, six of them at night.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: A Georgia Class D provisional license holder may not drive between which hours?","12:00 a.m. and 5:00 a.m., with no exceptions",["10:00 p.m. and 6:00 a.m.", "11:00 p.m. and 5:00 a.m., except for work", "1:00 a.m. and 4:00 a.m."],"Class D holders may not drive between midnight and 5:00 a.m. The manual says there are no exceptions.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: During the first six months of a Georgia Class D license, who may ride with the driver?","Only immediate family members",["Any passengers under 21", "One friend of any age", "Anyone, if all wear seat belts"],"For the first six months after issuance only immediate family members may ride in the vehicle.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: A person supervising a Georgia instructional permit holder must be at least what age and licensed for that class of vehicle?","21",["18", "25", "19"],"The permit holder must be accompanied by a person at least 21 who is licensed for a Class C vehicle and seated beside the driver.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you may not park within how many feet of a fire hydrant?","15 feet",["10 feet", "20 feet", "30 feet"],"Parking is prohibited within 15 feet of a fire hydrant.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you may not park within how many feet of a crosswalk at an intersection?","20 feet",["10 feet", "15 feet", "30 feet"],"Parking is prohibited within 20 feet of a crosswalk at an intersection.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you may not park within how many feet of a stop sign, yield sign or traffic signal?","30 feet",["15 feet", "20 feet", "50 feet"],"Parking is prohibited within 30 feet of a stop sign, yield sign or traffic control signal.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you may not park within how many feet of a railroad crossing?","50 feet",["15 feet", "30 feet", "100 feet"],"Parking is prohibited within 50 feet of a railroad crossing.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: When a Georgia railroad crossing signal is flashing or the gates are lowered, where must you stop?","Within 50 feet, but not less than 15 feet, from the nearest rail",["Right at the gate", "At least 100 feet away", "Anywhere before the tracks"],"You must stop within 50 feet but not less than 15 feet from the nearest rail.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you must dim your high beams within how many feet of an approaching vehicle?","500 feet",["200 feet", "300 feet", "1,000 feet"],"Use low beams within 500 feet of an approaching vehicle, and when following within 200 feet.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you must dim your high beams when following another vehicle within how many feet?","200 feet",["500 feet", "100 feet", "300 feet"],"Dim your lights when following closely, within 200 feet.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: For a Georgia driver 21 or older, what blood alcohol level is considered under the influence?","0.08 or more",["0.10 or more", "0.05 or more", "0.04 or more"],"A driver is considered under the influence when 0.08 grams or more by alcohol weight is present in the blood.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: For a Georgia driver under 21, what blood alcohol level is considered under the influence?","0.02 or more",["0.08 or more", "0.05 or more", "0.00 only"],"For drivers under 21 the limit is 0.02.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: A Georgia driver under 21 faces suspension for accumulating how many points within twelve months?","4 points",["15 points", "8 points", "2 points"],"Drivers under 21 are suspended for accumulating 4 points within twelve months.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: What does Georgia's Hands-Free Law prohibit?","Holding or supporting a phone for any reason while driving",["Talking through a wireless headset", "Using a mounted phone for navigation", "Listening to music"],"Drivers may not hold or support a phone. A phone may be used with headphones, a wireless device, a phone holder or a mounted device.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: What is the minimum legal space for a Georgia motorist passing a bicyclist?","3 feet",["1 foot", "5 feet", "10 feet"],"The minimum legal space to pass a bicyclist is 3 feet.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia, a child under what age must ride in an appropriate child passenger restraint system?","8 years",["5 years", "6 years", "10 years"],"Every driver transporting a child under eight must use a child restraint system appropriate for the child's height and weight, with limited exceptions.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: A new Georgia resident must get a Georgia license or permit within how many days?","30 days",["10 days", "60 days", "90 days"],"New residents must obtain a Georgia driver's license or permit within 30 days of becoming a resident.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: After a name or address change, a Georgia driver must update the license within how many days?","60 days",["10 days", "30 days", "90 days"],"You must update your address or obtain a license with the correct name within 60 days.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: Unless otherwise posted, what is the Georgia speed limit in an urban or residential district?","30 miles per hour",["25 miles per hour", "35 miles per hour", "45 miles per hour"],"The limit is 30 mph in any urban or residential district unless posted otherwise.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: Unless otherwise posted, what is the Georgia speed limit on a rural interstate?","70 miles per hour",["65 miles per hour", "75 miles per hour", "55 miles per hour"],"It is 70 mph on a rural interstate and 65 mph on an urban interstate or multi-lane divided highway.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: Unless otherwise posted, what is the Georgia speed limit on an unpaved county road?","35 miles per hour",["25 miles per hour", "45 miles per hour", "55 miles per hour"],"The limit on an unpaved county road is 35 mph.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: On a two-lane Georgia road, passing is prohibited within how many feet of a railroad crossing, bridge, viaduct or tunnel?","100 feet",["50 feet", "200 feet", "500 feet"],"Passing is prohibited within 100 feet of a railroad crossing and within 100 feet of a bridge, viaduct or tunnel.");
Q(12,10,2,"Georgia: In Georgia you may not park within how many feet of fire apparatus stopped in answer to a fire alarm?","500 feet",["100 feet", "200 feet", "50 feet"],"Do not park within 500 feet of fire apparatus stopped in answer to an alarm.");
/* Motorcycle add-on inside the driving app (domain 20) */
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Most of a motorcycle's stopping power comes from the","Front brake",["Rear brake", "Engine", "Clutch"],"The front brake gives about 70% or more of your stopping power.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: For the quickest safe stop, you should","Use both brakes at the same time",["Use the rear brake only", "Use the front brake only", "Pull in the clutch and coast"],"Apply both smoothly and firmly without locking a wheel.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The single most important piece of protective gear is","A helmet that meets DOT standards",["Leather gloves", "Riding boots", "A bright jacket"],"Head injuries are the main cause of rider deaths.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The best eye protection is","A face shield",["Regular eyeglasses", "Sunglasses", "A windshield alone"],"A shield protects your whole face from wind, dust and insects.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: To turn right at speed, you","Press forward on the right handgrip",["Press forward on the left handgrip", "Turn the handlebars sharply right", "Lean your body only"],"This is countersteering: press right, lean right, go right.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: When approaching a curve, you should","Slow down before the turn",["Brake hard in the middle of the turn", "Speed up as you enter", "Shift to neutral"],"Slow, look, press and roll on the throttle through the curve.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: In a turn, you should look","Through the turn to where you want to go",["At the road just ahead of the front wheel", "At the outside edge", "At your mirrors"],"Turn your head, not just your eyes. The motorcycle goes where you look.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Most crashes between a car and a motorcycle happen","At intersections",["On freeways", "In parking lots", "On curves in the country"],"The most common case is a car turning left in front of the rider.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: To be seen by other drivers, you should","Wear bright clothing and keep your headlight on",["Ride in the right edge of the lane", "Follow closely behind cars", "Ride only at night"],"Many drivers say they never saw the motorcycle.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Riding in a driver's blind spot is","Dangerous, because the driver may change lanes into you",["Safe if you match their speed", "Required in heavy traffic", "The best place to be seen"],"Move ahead or drop back so you appear in the mirrors.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A car and a motorcycle in the same lane","Each need a full lane width to be safe",["Can share the lane side by side", "Should share if traffic is slow", "Is required on freeways"],"Do not let drivers squeeze beside you. Ride where you protect your lane.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: On a slippery surface, you should","Slow down and avoid sudden moves",["Brake hard with the front brake", "Lean more in turns", "Speed up to get across"],"Keep the motorcycle as upright as you can.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: If your front wheel locks while braking, you should","Release the front brake at once, then reapply it smoothly",["Keep it locked until you stop", "Apply more rear brake", "Turn the handlebars"],"A locked front wheel will make you fall very quickly.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A passenger should","Lean with you and keep feet on the footrests",["Lean the opposite way in turns", "Put feet down at stops", "Sit as far back as possible"],"Tell your passenger to hold on, sit still and keep feet up even when stopped.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Carrying a passenger makes the motorcycle","Slower to stop, speed up and turn",["Stop faster", "Easier to balance at low speed", "Handle the same"],"Ride slower and leave more space.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The best formation for a group on a straight road is","Staggered",["Single file at all times", "Side by side in pairs", "Bunched close together"],"Staggering keeps the group close while giving each rider space.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: At night you should","Slow down and leave more space ahead",["Ride closer to the car ahead to see better", "Wear a tinted shield", "Use the low beam only"],"Use your high beam when no one is ahead or coming toward you.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Before every ride you should check","Tires, controls, lights, oil and chain",["Only the fuel level", "The paint", "The seat height"],"A quick walk-around catches problems before they cause a crash.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: For protection, besides a helmet you should wear","A jacket, long pants, gloves and boots that cover the ankle",["Shorts and sandals in summer", "A scarf and sneakers", "Whatever is comfortable"],"Good gear protects your skin in a slide and helps drivers see you.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A lane gives a motorcycle how many paths of travel?","Three: left, center and right",["One, in the center", "Two, left and right", "Four"],"Think of the lane as three positions and pick the one where you are seen best and have room to move.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The best lane position is the one that","Lets you be seen and gives you space to avoid hazards",["Is always the center", "Is always next to the curb", "Keeps you beside other vehicles"],"No single position is always best. Change position as traffic and the road change.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The oily strip in the center of a lane is usually","Safe to ride on unless the road is wet",["Too slippery to ever ride on", "The only safe place to ride", "Wider than the tire tracks"],"The center strip is usually no more than two feet wide. Avoid it in the first rain and at intersections where oil builds up.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: At an intersection, the greatest danger to a rider is usually","An oncoming car turning left across your path",["A car stopped behind you", "A parked car", "A car in the far lane going your way"],"Drivers turning left often fail to see a motorcycle. Slow down and be ready to stop or swerve.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Before changing lanes you should","Check your mirrors and turn your head to check the blind spot",["Check your mirrors only", "Signal and move at once", "Sound your horn"],"Motorcycle mirrors do not show everything. A head check is the only way to see a vehicle beside you.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Flashing your brake light before you slow down is most useful when","Someone is following closely or you are slowing where others do not expect it",["You are riding alone on an empty road", "You are speeding up", "You are parked"],"A few light taps on the brake warn the driver behind you.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: To stop quickly in a curve, the best method is to","Straighten the motorcycle first if you can, then brake hard",["Brake as hard as possible while leaned over", "Use only the rear brake", "Shift to neutral"],"If you cannot straighten up, brake smoothly and increase pressure as the motorcycle straightens.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: If you lock the rear wheel on a good surface, you should","Keep it locked until you have stopped",["Release it and stamp on it again", "Lean hard to one side", "Shift up a gear"],"Releasing a locked rear wheel while the motorcycle is out of line can throw you off. Keep it locked and steer straight.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Rolling on the throttle slightly through a turn","Helps keep the motorcycle stable",["Makes the motorcycle fall inward", "Is dangerous on dry roads", "Should only be done on hills"],"Steady or gently increasing throttle settles the suspension through the curve.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: In a slow, tight turn you should","Keep your body upright and let the motorcycle lean",["Lean your body far into the turn", "Stand on the footrests", "Brake hard with the front brake"],"In slow turns, counterbalance by keeping your body straight while the motorcycle leans.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A windshield on the motorcycle is","Not a substitute for a face shield or goggles",["Enough eye protection by itself", "Only needed at night", "A replacement for a helmet"],"Most windshields do not keep wind and debris out of your eyes.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A plastic face shield should be replaced when it is","Scratched enough to blur your vision",["One month old", "Clean", "Tinted"],"Scratches scatter light and can blind you at night or in sun.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Which helmet gives the most protection?","A full-face helmet that meets DOT standards",["A half helmet", "A bicycle helmet", "A cap worn under any helmet"],"A full-face helmet protects the chin and face as well as the skull. It must fit snugly and be fastened.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Groups of riders should keep","Small, so they are easier to pass and less likely to be split up",["As large as possible", "Side by side in each lane", "In single file at all times"],"If a group is larger than four or five, split it into smaller groups.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Riding side by side with another motorcycle in one lane is","Unsafe, because neither rider has room to move",["The best way to be seen", "Required in groups", "Safest at night"],"Each rider needs the full lane to swerve or avoid a hazard.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A group should pass another vehicle","One rider at a time",["All together", "Two at a time side by side", "On the shoulder"],"Each rider completes the pass and returns to position before the next one goes.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: When riding at night, you should use your high beam","Whenever you are not following or meeting another vehicle",["Never", "Only in town", "Only in rain"],"High beams let you see farther. Dim them for oncoming traffic and when following.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: To reduce fatigue on a long ride, you should","Take a rest break at least every two hours and limit how far you go in a day",["Ride faster to finish sooner", "Skip meals", "Avoid wind protection"],"Wind, cold and vibration tire you faster on a motorcycle than in a car.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: The front tire should be checked before each ride for","Air pressure, wear and damage",["Brand", "Color", "Age only"],"A tire with low pressure or damage can fail or handle badly.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: What following distance does the Georgia motorcycle manual teach?","At least four seconds",["One second", "Two car lengths", "Half a second"],"The manual uses a 4-second rule and says to open up more space when the road is slippery, when you cannot see through the vehicle ahead, or in heavy traffic.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: When railroad tracks cross your lane at an angle, it is usually safer to","Ride straight across within your lane",["Swerve to cross at exactly 90 degrees", "Brake hard on the tracks", "Cross on the shoulder"],"The manual warns that turning to take tracks at 90 degrees can be more dangerous, because your path may carry you into another lane of traffic.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: For tracks and road seams that run parallel to your course, you should","Move far enough away to cross them at an angle",["Ride along the top of the rail", "Cross them as slowly as you can at a shallow angle", "Ignore them"],"A tire can catch on an edge it meets at a shallow angle. Move away, then cross at a clear angle.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: When riders in a group follow one another, they should keep a minimum following distance of","Two seconds",["Half a second", "One car length", "Five seconds"],"The manual's group riding rules say to keep a minimum two-second following distance and ride staggered.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: If you need to stop while leaned over in a curve, you should","Apply smooth, gradual pressure to both brakes as you reduce your lean",["Grab the front brake hard", "Use only the rear brake", "Shift to neutral and coast"],"The more you reduce the lean, the more traction you have for braking, so add brake pressure as the motorcycle straightens.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A passenger should keep both feet","On the footrests, even when the motorcycle is stopped",["On the ground at stops", "On the exhaust pipes", "Dangling to help balance"],"The manual tells passengers to keep feet firmly on the footrests even when stopped and to keep legs away from mufflers, chains and moving parts.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Where should a passenger hold on?","Your waist or hips, or the passenger handholds",["The handlebars", "Your shoulders only", "Nothing: holding on is unsafe"],"A firm hold on the rider's waist or hips, or the handholds, keeps the passenger stable when you brake or accelerate.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Before carrying a passenger or heavy load, you should check the owner's manual because","Extra weight changes how the motorcycle handles and the suspension may need adjusting",["Passengers are illegal on most motorcycles", "The engine must be rebuilt", "It changes nothing"],"The manual says extra weight affects operation and to adjust the motorcycle as the owner's manual directs.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Which statement about tinted eye protection is correct?","It should not be worn at night or when there is little light",["It is best at night", "It replaces a helmet", "It is required at all times"],"Tinted shields and glasses cut the light you need to see in the dark.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Long-term exposure to wind noise on a motorcycle can","Cause permanent hearing damage",["Improve your hearing", "Do nothing", "Only affect passengers"],"Properly worn hearing protection reduces wind noise and still lets you hear horns and sirens.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Are jeans enough leg protection for riding?","No. Jeans do not provide adequate protection",["Yes, any jeans are enough", "Yes, if they are new", "Only in winter"],"The manual says sturdy synthetic or leather riding gear protects best and that jeans do not provide adequate protection.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: In Georgia, a motorcycle rider must wear","A helmet that meets DOT standards",["Any hat with a chin strap", "A helmet only on interstates", "A helmet only if under 21"],"The manual states that Georgia requires a DOT compliant helmet.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: In Georgia, a motorcycle's headlight and taillight must be","On at all times",["On only at night", "On only in rain", "On only on highways"],"The manual lists that the headlight and taillight must be illuminated at all times.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: In Georgia, how far before a left turn may you enter the center turn lane?","No more than 300 feet",["No more than 100 feet", "Up to half a mile", "Any distance"],"Georgia law limits the center lane to left turns, and you may enter it no more than 300 feet from the turn.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Can you be convicted of riding impaired in Georgia with a blood alcohol level under .08?","Yes, if you are impaired",["No, never", "Only if you crash", "Only if you are under 21"],"The manual says that even under .08 you can be impaired and convicted of riding impaired.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: A typical drink contains about how much alcohol?","Half an ounce",["Two ounces", "A full ounce and a half", "None, if it is beer"],"A typical drink, such as one shot of spirits, has about half an ounce of alcohol.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: If a driver is tailgating your motorcycle, the best choice is to","Change lanes and let them pass, or slow down to open more space ahead",["Speed up to get away", "Ignore them", "Brake hard to warn them"],"Letting the tailgater by, or adding space ahead so you can stop gradually, removes the danger.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: What do the letters in the riding strategy SEE stand for?","Search, Evaluate, Execute",["Stop, Enter, Exit", "Signal, Engage, Ease", "Speed, Energy, Escape"],"Riders are taught to search for hazards, evaluate what could happen, and execute a response, always with an escape route.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: An escape route is","An alternate path you can take if a hazard develops",["The shoulder of the road only", "The lane behind you", "A route with no traffic lights"],"The manual says to always use SEE and plan an escape route, whatever the conditions.");
Q(12,20,1,"Motorcycle: Successfully completing an approved Georgia motorcycle safety course can earn you","A license test waiver",["A commercial license", "Lower speed limits", "An automatic helmet exemption"],"The Georgia Motorcycle Safety Program course provides training and a License Test Waiver when completed successfully.");
